    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7e21a551-a24d-3b43-bc81-dcbcf90336c3",
                "word": "messuage",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3112ecb5-1835-4427-98d7-d70ae2fc7a39",
                        "entry_id": "7e21a551-a24d-3b43-bc81-dcbcf90336c3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "messuages"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34d9e0f7-7ae5-32af-ba06-71c5d731b7e6",
                        "entry_id": "7e21a551-a24d-3b43-bc81-dcbcf90336c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Originally, a plot of land as the site for a dwelling house and its appurtenant interests; now, a dwelling house or residential building together with its outbuildings and assigned land."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "91f39afe-fecf-43bd-9dd5-25164160fab8",
                                "sense_id": "34d9e0f7-7ae5-32af-ba06-71c5d731b7e6",
                                "text": "Dying intestate, Juan was sole heir / To a chancery suit, and messuages, and lands, / Which, with a long minority and care, / Promised to turn out well in proper hands: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbb881ef-0a9c-4778-b862-3ed6aa85d4b0",
                                "sense_id": "34d9e0f7-7ae5-32af-ba06-71c5d731b7e6",
                                "text": "And be it further ordained and enacted by the Authority aforesaid, That the Right and Title of the said Ecclesiastics of the Seminary of Saint Sulpice of Montreal, in and to all and singular the said Fiefs and Seigniories of the Island of Montreal, of the Lake of the Two Mountains, and of Saint Sulpice, and their several Dependencies, and in and to all Seigniorial and Feudal Rights, Privileges, Dues, and Duties arising out of and from the same, and in and to all and every the Domains, Lands, Reservations, Buildings, Messuages, Tenements, and Hereditaments within the said several Fiefs and Seigniories now held and possessed by them as Proprietors thereof, […] shall be and they are hereby confirmed and declared good, valid, and effectual in the Law; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b757f6f-ab29-46b9-a969-986c9f6ce421",
                                "sense_id": "34d9e0f7-7ae5-32af-ba06-71c5d731b7e6",
                                "text": "She went—and in one month / They wedded her to sixty thousand pounds, / To lands in Kent and messuages in York, / And slight Sir Robert with his watery smile / And educated whisker."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a408af5-5083-4ade-87a1-09fc4b23a38c",
                                "sense_id": "34d9e0f7-7ae5-32af-ba06-71c5d731b7e6",
                                "text": "Page 174, line 25. Perhaps the Richard Longebothome here mentioned was the same man as the Richard who herioted the property in 1509. Apr. 23, I Hen. VIII (1509). Ric. Longebothome paid xxiijˢ iiijᵈ [23s 4d] fine for license of herioting one messuage called Longebothome, one cottage, and 40 acres of land and meadow in Soureby after the death of Ric. Longebothome and Agnes, his wife, grandfather […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "123abaa5-661c-44d2-8b65-a9be8dee2775",
                                "sense_id": "34d9e0f7-7ae5-32af-ba06-71c5d731b7e6",
                                "text": "Matthias turned his lonely house into a mart where furniture, plate and titledeeds to fields and messuages could be brought, evaluated, and transferred to the hands of the primal twelve as administrators."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b833e057-e149-40b4-b509-9e7108acd42f",
                        "source_entry_id": "7e21a551-a24d-3b43-bc81-dcbcf90336c3",
                        "source_sense_id": "34d9e0f7-7ae5-32af-ba06-71c5d731b7e6",
                        "source_sense_description": "dwelling house or land",
                        "target_lang_word": "Anwesen",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Anwesen",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b915f875-2b0c-356d-bbd5-5bff9cd80f03",
                                        "entry_id": "35103844-f8aa-354e-bfaa-b033b6e25872",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gesamtheit eines zusammenhängenden Immobilienbesitzes; als Wohnsitz genutztes, bebautes Grundstück"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02260a91-82d5-497e-8fdb-755355a58a1f",
                                                "sense_id": "b915f875-2b0c-356d-bbd5-5bff9cd80f03",
                                                "text": "Nachdem sie im Lotto gewonnen hatten, konnten sie ein riesiges Anwesen ihr Eigen nennen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a907d9a-645c-4cc0-8f20-deae75924d7f",
                                                "sense_id": "b915f875-2b0c-356d-bbd5-5bff9cd80f03",
                                                "text": "„Jetzt nahm ich mir die Zeit, das Anwesen genauer zu betrachten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a92f030-6fde-470b-966f-134db2720195",
                                                "sense_id": "b915f875-2b0c-356d-bbd5-5bff9cd80f03",
                                                "text": "„Es ist wie ein großes Anwesen, dessen Herr für immer abgereist ist.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "554a846f-b1fe-4745-a63b-485e1c461011",
                                                "sense_id": "b915f875-2b0c-356d-bbd5-5bff9cd80f03",
                                                "text": "„Das Anwesen hatte eine vierräumige Straßenfront und bestand aus drei hinter einander gelegenen Räumlichkeiten in der Tiefe.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53091c26-3e44-43d0-b8f9-0fca45129e7f",
                                                "sense_id": "b915f875-2b0c-356d-bbd5-5bff9cd80f03",
                                                "text": "„Die Hieroglyphe stellt einen klar umgrenzten, also geschützten Raum mit einer Türöffnung dar; es dürfte sich wohl eher um ein ganzes Anwesen als nur um ein einfaches Haus handeln.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
